    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "recap",
      "narration_text": "So far, my papers looked at uncertainty from environmental science and risk assessment. This week, I turned to uncertainty inside A I itself.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B01_Turn",
        "visual_intent": "From environmental science to AI.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.66
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "literature review",
      "narration_text": "My sixth paper is A Review of Uncertainty Quantification in Deep Learning: Techniques, Applications and Challenges, by Abdar, Pourpanah, Hussain and colleagues, published in Information Fusion in twenty twenty one.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B02_Paper",
        "visual_intent": "Citation card for paper 6.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.19
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "motivation",
      "narration_text": "The authors review techniques to estimate, quantify, and manage uncertainty in deep learning. Their motivation: A I is increasingly used for real world predictions and decisions, but its outputs can't always be assumed to be reliable.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B03_Motivation",
        "visual_intent": "Network → prediction → decision: reliable?",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.68
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "motivation",
      "narration_text": "A model may make a prediction without adequately representing how uncertain it is about that prediction.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B04_Missing",
        "visual_intent": "A prediction with no uncertainty attached.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 5.93
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "methods",
      "narration_text": "The review covers approaches such as Bayesian methods, ensemble learning, and other techniques that estimate uncertainty in model predictions.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B05_Methods",
        "visual_intent": "Bayesian · ensembles · other.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.58
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "two sources",
      "narration_text": "These methods can help separate cases where the model has limited knowledge, from cases where the input data themselves are noisy or inherently uncertain.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B06_TwoSources",
        "visual_intent": "Limited knowledge vs noisy data.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.94
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "applications",
      "narration_text": "The paper also looks at applications across domains, including computer vision, medical applications, natural language processing, and other scientific fields.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B07_Domains",
        "visual_intent": "Four application domains.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.41
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "takeaway",
      "narration_text": "A major takeaway: uncertainty estimation is not simply about making a model produce a confidence number.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B08_NotANumber",
        "visual_intent": "More than a number.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 6.7
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "takeaway",
      "narration_text": "It means choosing appropriate techniques, understanding their limitations, and evaluating whether the estimates are useful for the intended application. The authors also highlight open challenges for making deep learning more reliable.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B09_Steps",
        "visual_intent": "Choose · understand · evaluate.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.78
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "insight",
      "narration_text": "For my research, this paper is the technical bridge. Environmental research has methods for understanding uncertainty, and A I research has methods for estimating it in predictions.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B10_Bridge",
        "visual_intent": "Two fields, one bridge.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.78
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "insight",
      "narration_text": "The key question is how these two areas work together.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B11_Gap",
        "visual_intent": "The bridge is incomplete.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 3.11
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "act": "example",
      "narration_text": "An A I may have a technically derived uncertainty estimate for its prediction, but that estimate may not reflect the quality of an environmental disclosure, the uncertainty in an emissions calculation, or a conflict between corporate reports.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B12_Disconnect",
        "visual_intent": "Model estimate vs evidence problems.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.06
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "act": "direction",
      "narration_text": "So my research direction is: can A I uncertainty quantification be meaningfully connected to environmental evidence quality and assessment uncertainty, rather than being treated as an independent, model generated score?",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "af_bella",
      "shot": {
        "type": "MANIM",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": "scenes.py::B13_Direction",
        "visual_intent": "Connect, not independent.",
        "show": []
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.38
    },
    {
